Z||000011||BBBAD GT||08-04-2000||02:02 PM||||A little word about fuel pumps.  I'm not sure what is on the Fiero stock, but a 255l is more than enough for ANY motor you can shoe in the Fiero.  You will most likely run into line restrictions before maxing out a 255l.<P>If the Mustang fuel pump does fit a Fiero, then I'll give a little more info on Mustang pumps:<P>There is a wide range of pumps for the Stang, from 110/155/190/255l.  There are two kinds of 255l out there, one that is good for high pressure applications (more desirable), and the other for standard pressure (around 40psi).  The price difference between all the pumps is like $15 between them.  Some blown Stangs run two pumps in series (normally Vortech's T-rex) with good results.  The problem Stangs are running into is line/rail restriction.  In my case, I went with a full blown boogie fuel system, with a 450+l exteranl fuel pump, -10 feed and -8 return lines, with 5/8" rails and 36lb injectors.  The pump is only rated to continuesly run for only 5 hours, which I've put a voltage reducer so it wouldn't work as hard on the street but keep adequate pressure.<P>One theory people say if you go waay over on the pump capacity, then you are just heating the fuel by returning most of it via return line.  I don't know if its true or not, but anybody changing fuel pumps in Stangs are putting in the 255l with no problems, and are only worried about matching injectors to around 450 hp.<P>Sorry for the rambling.........<P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierocrazy||08-04-2000||05:10 PM||||i have a cammed out 3.2 and it runs at 35pounds,,, so a new 2.8 will work,, unlesss you are going to add turbo or nitros, i went with a 91 corvette pump and an adjustable regulator.  which maxes at 50 pounds.  which my 3.8 injectors will float them at 40 pounds,, So I cant imagine 2.8 injectors do any better, i guess I am saying going with a 76pound pump doesnt make sense when your injectors will float at somewhere around 36 pounds ......... mine works great||||reg||1
Z||000013||HYPTNOTiSE||08-04-2000||06:26 PM||||I've done my research on this.  Holley sells walboro pumps, but with their name on them. GN's, f-body(camaro/firebirds), eagle talons, and fieros use the same size fuel pump. you can get a "universal" pump(not that it's not specifically designed for the fiero, but it's universal cos all those cars use the same setup) from Granitelli motorsports through summit for 99 bucks. it's 255lph, the only way you'd max that pump out would be to put an injected small block with a blower and nitrous. And if you have that setup, you wouldn't be too worried about how much a fuel pump costs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Hope that helps, once again another reason i'd never buy something from the fiero store again. I could order things(not even wholesale) from summit and carparts.com and if i got the same amount of orders that the fiero store does, and i charged their prices i bet i'd make over 30K  a year.||||reg||1
Z||000014||BBBAD GT||08-04-2000||06:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierocrazy:<BR><B>which my 3.8 injectors will float them at 40 pounds,, So I cant imagine 2.8 injectors do any better, i guess I am saying going with a 76pound pump doesnt make sense when your injectors will float at somewhere around 36 pounds ......... mine works great</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm a little confused, what do you mean by <B>float the injectors</B>?  Do you mean when they go 100% duty cycle, so they are basically 'open' the whole time?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||88 Fiero GT Turbo||08-05-2000||05:39 PM||||Ok guys are we saying that the fuel pumps in the grand national, camaros, and Fiero's are all the same????<P><BR>Later,<BR>Jack||||reg||1
Z||000016||fierocrazy||08-06-2000||01:13 AM||||Float the injector = When fuel flow is so high that the injector cant cut the pulse off||||reg||1
